+# Speech batches in Jobs & Recovery (v7.0.83)
+
+## What was wrong (reported on 7.0.82)
+
+1. **"Correct them in step 4"** appeared in Jobs & Recovery for a job whose Create page had no step 4. The job's
+   TTS step regenerated the Odia narration in the job folder and ignored the narration approved in Create step 4.
+   There was no editing control on the page the message sent the user to.
+2. **Halfway-failed jobs were invisible.** Create's Prepare step (and a job's TTS step before the job record exists)
+   writes its batch under `speech_preparation/`. Jobs & Recovery listed only folders with a
+   `production_manifest.json`, so a batch that stopped after one or two TTS calls had no row.
+3. `approve_localized_scripts` (Create step 4) did not run the script check, so the Odia text with
+   foreign letters could be approved and the error appeared only at TTS time.
+
+## What changed
+
+- **Job reruns use the approved narration.** `prepare_batch` takes the narration saved by Create step 4
+  (`speech_preparation/scripts/<key>/localized_scripts.json`) when it exists. It regenerates narration only when no
+  approved narration exists for that master and language set.
+- **Batches are recorded from the start.** `batch.json` stores the narration, the request settings (TTS provider,
+  narration audio, cleanup, text cards, educational, topic, card provider, hooks) and the last error. A batch that
+  stops is kept with its error.
+- **Approval checks script words.** Create step 4 refuses a language narration that contains words outside its script,
+  with the same rule as before TTS. English words and brand names are not flagged.
+- **Jobs & Recovery → Speech batches.** Lists Create step 4 batches and unfinished batches inside jobs, with the
+  error, per-language narration (editable, with a review checkbox for each non-master language), **Save corrected
+  narration** and **Resume TTS and cards**. The message no longer names a page the user may not have. A wrong-script
+  error now reads: correct it in Jobs & Recovery > Speech batches (or Create step 4), save, then resume.
+- **Resume.** Uses the saved narration and settings. Languages with a voice file already on disk are reused, so only
+  unfinished languages are sent to TTS. A corrected batch clears its old voice files, so an old voice for the old
+  text cannot be attached.
+
+## Limits
+
+- A job with no approved narration still generates narration when its TTS step runs (as before). Always approve
+  narration in Create step 4 for Odia and Hindi jobs.
+- Gemini request limits still apply to each resume. The Speech batches panel does not check quota before resuming;
+  see the 7.0.81 and 7.0.82 notes for daily-limit behaviour.
+
+## Files
+
+- `engine/speech_cards.py`: `reviewed_scripts_for`, `prepare_batch` (saves state, approved narration, error),
+  `approve_localized_scripts` (script check).
+- `engine/speech_batches.py` (new): `list_speech_batches`, `correct_speech_scripts`, `resume_speech_batch`.
+- `app.py`: Jobs & Recovery (Queue page) Speech batches panel.
+- `tests/test_v783_speech_batches.py` (new, 6 tests).
+- `tools/update_v782_to_v783.py`: updater from 7.0.82. Earlier steps are in earlier release zips.
